      "message": "`slugify` now transliterates accented letters instead of dropping them: `café` gives `cafe`. All three tests in `tests/test_core.py` pass.\n\nThe change is in `slug/core.py`. Each character is decomposed with Unicode NFKD and the combining accent marks are removed, so `é`, `ü`, and similar letters map to their base letters. A small table covers letters that don't decompose, so `ß` becomes `ss`, `æ` becomes `ae`, and `ø`, `ł`, `đ`, and `œ` map to `o`, `l`, `d`, and `oe`. Other non-ASCII letters with no ASCII equivalent are still dropped, and non-letter symbols still become dashes, as before.\n\nI also added `test_accented_letters_are_transliterated` to `tests/test_core.py`, covering `café`, `Crème Brûlée`, and `Straße Æther`. Nothing has been committed.",
